        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.282,
            0.764,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": "Can you explain how the mean is the centre of each collection?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.308,
            0.802,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": "Is the mean the midpoint of the two endpoints/extremes of the data? It is not always so. Instead, the total distances are equal on both the sides of the mean. This is illustrated through the following dot plots."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.405,
            0.469,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.497,
            0.385,
            0.873,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.534,
            0.479,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_chart_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "bbox": [
            0.521,
            0.53,
